<section id="about" class="about">
  <h2 class="sec-h">About</h2>
  <p>I build the backend parts of software that people only notice when they break, and I try hard to make sure they don't.</p>
  <p>
    For seven years that meant <strong>Vocera's clinical communication platform</strong>: the APIs, message
    queues and Linux servers that get alerts and calls to hospital staff. I started there part-time in 2014,
    while finishing my degree, and left in 2021 as a platform developer and scrum master for an international team.
  </p>
  <p>
    In 2026 I was COO and technical lead at ME Tech, a five-person software contracting company in Japan. There I
    upgraded a school management platform from Rails 4.2 to Rails 7.1, step by step, with more than 8,000 tests
    that I built with Claude Code and reviewed. On my own time I've been building Sensei Connect, a bilingual
    marketplace for substitute and on-demand teachers in Japan, and smaller things I want to exist, like a
    companion app for Heartopia players.
  </p>
  <p>
    I build with Claude Code, on my side projects including this site and on client work at ME Tech. I set the
    architecture, design and test plan, Claude Code writes most of the code, and I review every change against
    the tests. I can explain any decision in it.
  </p>
  <p>
    I've taught English in Osaka since 2024, to students from one to sixty-five. Planning a lesson and designing an
    API turn out to be the same job: know who is in front of you and give them the right abstraction.
  </p>
</section>
